# Summary
Introduced a delayed authorization check for streaming PutObject, allowing extra body ingestion before access denial.
The new fast path removes the early begin_stream_put call from prepare_streaming_put and stores only the principal/ACL headers. Authorization and bucket write reservation now happen later in start_streaming_put_session, which is invoked only after the request body fills the internal segment buffer. As a result, a client with valid credentials but without write permission can cause the server to read and buffer up to INTERNAL_SEGMENT_SIZE (8 MiB) of data before the access check fails, increasing bandwidth/CPU usage and enabling low-effort availability degradation.

# Validation
## Rubric
- [x] Identify where streaming PutObject authorization is enforced (begin_stream_put) and confirm it checks write permission.
- [x] Confirm prepare_streaming_put no longer calls begin_stream_put and only stores principal/ACL.
- [x] Trace streaming ingest to show buffering up to INTERNAL_SEGMENT_SIZE before session creation.
- [x] Verify INTERNAL_SEGMENT_SIZE value (8 MiB) to quantify pre-auth ingestion.
- [ ] Reproduce dynamically with debug build/PoC (blocked by missing libisal and unavailable valgrind/gdb).
## Report
Crash attempt: `cargo build -p argmin-s3` failed because `ec-sys` requires the system `libisal` (missing `libisal.pc`), so no binary was produced for a crash PoC. `valgrind` and `gdb` are not installed in the container, blocking those methods. Code validation: `prepare_streaming_put` constructs `StreamingPutContext` without calling `begin_stream_put`, while `start_streaming_put_session` later invokes `coordinator.begin_stream_put` with requester/ACL info (crates/server-http/src/http/mod.rs:2375-2412). The streaming handler reads body frames and calls `ingest_streaming_put_payload` after `prepare_streaming_put` returns (crates/server-http/src/http/serve.rs:1136-1223). Inside `ingest_streaming_put_payload`, the buffer is filled until it reaches `INTERNAL_SEGMENT_SIZE`; only then does it call `append_streaming_put_buffer`, which calls `ensure_streaming_put_session` and thus `start_streaming_put_session` (crates/server-http/src/http/serve.rs:1520-1709). `begin_stream_put` is where write authorization is enforced, returning `AccessDenied` if the requester lacks write permission (crates/server-core/src/coordinator.rs:3682-3689). `INTERNAL_SEGMENT_SIZE` is 8 MiB (crates/server-core/src/coordinator.rs:45). Therefore an authenticated but unauthorized client can force the server to read/buffer up to 8 MiB before the access check fails, matching the suspected availability impact.

